## Why This Is Asked

This angle tests end-to-end system thinking across multilingual NLP, streaming latency, privacy-by-design, RAG, and deployment.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual intent classifier with adapters trained on English/Spanish/Japanese corpora
- Streaming ASR integration and latency budgets (target ~150 ms)
- Privacy: data minimization, on-device processing where possible, PII masking, tenant isolation
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation for consistent responses
- Deployment: feature flags, drift monitoring, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code illustrating a multilingual intent classifier with adapters
const { Tokenizer, Model } = require('transformers-js');
const tokenizer = Tokenizer.fromPretrained('xlm-roberta-base');
const model = Model.fromPretrained('xlm-roberta-base', { numLabels: 50 });
model.addAdapter('multilingual');
model.setActiveAdapters(['multilingual']);
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor model drift across languages and handle changes in intents?
- How would you design a safe fallback path when the classifier has low confidence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design latency-aware, privacy-preserving, multilingual systems that justify decisions rather than just detect. Emphasizes RAG, policy integration, and drift handling across many languages.

## Key Concepts
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) vs pure classifiers
- On-device first-pass with quantized transformers
- Privacy: differential privacy, encrypted policy KB, secure inference
- Multilingual handling and code-switching
- Drift detection, rollout strategies, rollback plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo architecture sketch
class Detector {
  constructor(){ /* load on-device model */ }
  async predict(msg){
    const lang = identifyLanguage(msg);
    const local = await runOnDevice(msg, lang);
    const refs = await fetchPolicyRefs(msg, lang); // retrieval
    const rationale = buildRAG(refs, local);
    const cloudOut = await cloudInfer(msg, rationale);
    return { label: cloudOut.label, rationale };
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate policy-ref quality and latency separately?
- How would you handle a new language with minimal data and ensure privacy material?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical, on-device NLP that yields actionable summaries from multilingual consumer reviews, a realistic Instacart/Amazon use case, without network dependency.

## Key Concepts
- On-device multilang NLP under tight size constraints
- Feature extraction via lightweight POS or rules
- Sentiment aggregation and justification
- Privacy-first data labeling and offline evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreFeature(feature, sentences) {
  let score = 0;
  for (const s of sentences) {
    if (s.toLowerCase().includes(feature)) {
      if (/\b(good|great|excellent|loved)\b/.test(s)) score += 1;
      if (/\b(bad|worst|terrible|hate)\b/.test(s)) score -= 1;
    }
  }
  return score;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle negation and language switch within a single sentence?
- How would you validate usefulness of summaries to buyers?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical NLP task: normalize product names across languages in chat, a common customer-support need.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual dictionary-based normalization
- Code-switching handling via token-level language tagging
- Lightweight fuzzy matching (Levenshtein) for typos
- In-browser latency constraints and basic privacy controls
- Per-language evaluation plan

## Code Example

```javascript
const dict = {
  en: { "iphone": "IPHON-X" },
  es: { "iphone": "IPHON-X" },
  de: { "iphone": "IPHON-X" }
};

function normalize(token, lang){
  const d = dict[lang] || {};
  if (d[token]) return { canonical_id: d[token], conf: 1.0 };
  // simple fallback: lowercasing + basic similarity could be added here
  return { canonical_id: token, conf: 0.5 };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to add new product names without retraining?
- How to detect language and manage code-switching at runtime?
- How to scale dictionaries across dozens of languages while preserving privacy?
